This licence covers the firmware source in this repository, namely the
Platform/ and Silicon/ trees, the scripts under scripts/, the EDK2 patches
under patches/firmware/, and the documentation.

Portions of this work are derived from EDK2 and edk2-platforms and retain
the copyright notices of their original authors -- including Intel
Corporation, Arm Limited, Linaro Ltd, Red Hat Inc., Semihalf, Advanced Micro
Devices Inc., Qualcomm Technologies Inc., Hewlett Packard Enterprise, Jeremy
Linton, and Microsoft Corporation.  Those notices appear in the individual
files and are unaffected by this one.  All such material is likewise
BSD-2-Clause-Patent.

Also note, on the display code: the HDMI/VPU register sequences in
Platform/Khadas/Vim3/Drivers/MesonDisplayDxe were reimplemented against the
public A311D datasheet with reference to the BSD-3-Clause Amlogic display
and DesignWare HDMI drivers in Fuchsia (Copyright The Fuchsia Authors).  No
Fuchsia code is reproduced, but the derivation is acknowledged.

Six things this licence does NOT cover:

  * Vendor firmware blobs (BL2/DDR, BL30, BL31) obtained from LibreELEC's
    amlogic-boot-fip repository.  These are redistributed under their own
    terms and are not licensed by this project.  They are not contained in
    this repository; they are fetched from the pinned submodule at build
    time.

  * Linux kernel patches under patches/linux/ and patches/upstream/, and the
    out-of-tree kernel modules under patches/linux/g12b-cpufreq/,
    patches/linux/g12b-pcie-acpi/ and patches/linux/vim3-hdmi-snd/, all of
    which are GPL-2.0 as derivatives of the Linux kernel.

  * patches/linux/hevc/ -- two never-merged patches by Maxime Jourdan
    <mjourdan@baylibre.com> and Benjamin Roszak <benjamin545@gmail.com>,
    reproduced as carried by LibreELEC.  GPL-2.0, copyright their authors.
    patches/linux/0024 squashes these together with our own changes; the
    original authors are credited in that patch's commit message.

  * patches/firmware/edk2/0002 (UsbBusDxe enumeration retry), by Jared Pan
    <jared.pan@dell.com>, and patches/linux/0006 (stmmac ACPI glue), by
    Ricardo Pardini <ricardo@pardini.net> for Armbian.  Copyright their
    authors, under the licence of the projects they patch.

  * The change made by patches/linux/0005 (arm64/efi SW-PAN), which was
    proposed by Will Deacon <will@kernel.org> in review on the linux-efi
    list and is carried here with a Suggested-by: trailer.  It is now
    upstream, authored by him, as commit e98a9d014637 in Linux v7.3-rc1.
    GPL-2.0, as a derivative of the Linux kernel.

  * ffmpeg patches under patches/userspace/ffmpeg/.  ffmpeg is licensed
    LGPL-2.1-or-later, with some components GPL-2.0-or-later, and these
    patches inherit the licence of the files they modify.  Patch 0001 in
    particular is NOT our work: it is a subset of John Cox's V4L2 M2M
    rework from jc-kynesim/rpi-ffmpeg, with his code unaltered.  See the
    header of that patch, and patches/userspace/ffmpeg/README.md, for full
    provenance.

